{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"81bb014e710a6b95","name":"card_unit_989_infantry_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WorldAtWar/units/card_unit_989_infantry_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"989. INFANTRY REGIMENT","text":"Deployment: Gets +2+2 if this is your only unit.","flavorText":"The 989th Grenadier Regiment was a unit of the 277th Infantry Division of the Wehrmacht. The regiment was formed in 1943 in Croatia, and shortly after it was relocated to France, along with the 277th Division. In August 1944 the division participated in the Battle of Normandy where it was destroyed, but reformed in September 1944 and sent to defend against the Allied advance in Northern France and Rhineland. After that the regiment participated in the Ardennes Offensive where it fought with the 12th Volksgrenadier Division in an attempt to capture the Belgian towns of Rocherath-Krinkelt and Elsenborn, in what is now known as the Battle of the Bulge. During the battle the regiment suffered heavy losses and was forced to retreat into Germany where it continued fighting, mostly with new and inexperienced recruits, and by the end of March in 1944 the regiment had been defeated.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_989_infantry_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_989_infantry_regiment_title","SourceString":"989. INFANTRY REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"989. INFANTRY REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_989_infantry_regiment_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Gets +2+2 if this is your only unit.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Gets +2+2 if this is your only unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_989_infantry_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 989th Grenadier Regiment was a unit of the 277th Infantry Division of the Wehrmacht. The regiment was formed in 1943 in Croatia, and shortly after it was relocated to France, along with the 277th Division. In August 1944 the division participated in the Battle of Normandy where it was destroyed, but reformed in September 1944 and sent to defend against the Allied advance in Northern France and Rhineland. After that the regiment participated in the Ardennes Offensive where it fought with the 12th Volksgrenadier Division in an attempt to capture the Belgian towns of Rocherath-Krinkelt and Elsenborn, in what is now known as the Battle of the Bulge. During the battle the regiment suffered heavy losses and was forced to retreat into Germany where it continued fighting, mostly with new and inexperienced recruits, and by the end of March in 1944 the regiment had been defeated.","LocalizedString":"The 989th Grenadier Regiment was a unit of the 277th Infantry Division of the Wehrmacht. The regiment was formed in 1943 in Croatia, and shortly after it was relocated to France, along with the 277th Division. In August 1944 the division participated in the Battle of Normandy where it was destroyed, but reformed in September 1944 and sent to defend against the Allied advance in Northern France and Rhineland. After that the regiment participated in the Ardennes Offensive where it fought with the 12th Volksgrenadier Division in an attempt to capture the Belgian towns of Rocherath-Krinkelt and Elsenborn, in what is now known as the Battle of the Bulge. During the battle the regiment suffered heavy losses and was forced to retreat into Germany where it continued fighting, mostly with new and inexperienced recruits, and by the end of March in 1944 the regiment had been defeated."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Blitz","EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"